"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act5_ch28.md — do not edit */

SC["a5c28_debt"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWENTY-EIGHT — THE WEAVER'S DEBT`)+P(`A truth only one living person can see is testimony, not evidence. You learned that watching the inquest drown in clean paper. So you spend two of your six days making the Between's needlework CHECKABLE, and the tool for it has been sitting in a shrine-niche all along, black with age, keeping the Court's own perfect books.`)+P(`The index. Four hundred years of consignment records — and every record names an INTAKE SITE. Where each foreign soul was found: which riverbank, which marsh, which village with souring nets. Ruan transcribes; Suyin maps each site against the warp's own tension-charts, forty years of fray-edge surveys in the Court's own hand; you stand at the wall where the two papers meet, and watch four centuries of theology come apart at one seam.`)+P(`Every site sits on thin cloth. Every one. A thousand souls a generation, and not one ever arrived on sound sky — they land along the Fray's hem like stitches in a mending-run, in ORDER, the intake dates marching down the tear's length the way a needle marches down a seam. The correlation isn't a tendency. It's a SIGNATURE: the Between, sewing, patiently, forever, into the exact holes — and a Court of honest bookkeepers netting each patch as it landed, calling the mending an infestation, and burning it to keep a dead machine warm.`)+P(`Ruan sets down his brush when the last site is plotted, and for once in his measured life he says the total out loud, unrounded: “They were never wounds. They were the SUTURES. We have been harvesting the medicine for four hundred years.” He looks at his own hands. “My master sold the medicine, brother. By the BALE.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The Lady has to see this wall.`,do:()=>{G.f.a5_truth=true;},go:"a5c28_lady"}]};

SC["a5c28_lady"]={t:()=>P(`You bring the First Reel to the wall the only way she can come: Suyin carries the small black reel from its shrine-niche and sets it on the table, and the Lady reads the two mapped papers through it in a silence that goes on so long the lamp needs trimming twice.`)+P(`“Say it,” she says at last. The everywhere-voice, down to one small reel on one table, very quiet. “You have earned the saying of it. Say it plainly.”`)+P(`“The fraying calls them, Lady. The Between sews loose souls where the cloth is thinnest — that is what the Between is FOR. They arrive at the tear because they are sent to the tear. Four hundred years ago a sky fell on you, and heaven itself started sending you thread —” you put your finger on the first intake record, dated four months after her Loom first stood — “and you caught it, and weighed it, and burned it, and the hole you were holding shut never once stopped being fed the very mending you were feeding to the machine.”`)+P(`The reel turns once. Stops. When the voice comes again it has nothing in it at all, which from her is a scream.`)+P(`“I ANSWERED the tear. I was the only one who answered.” Another turn, slower. “And every answer heaven sent after me, I filed as a symptom.” The lamp burns. Somewhere above, ten thousand reels keep breathing. “Four hundred years, little stitch, I asked every generation for a competent wrongness, and I was the wrongness, and the competence took this long to walk in off a riverbank.” The black reel turns a third time, and now you hear it: not grief. RELIEF, terrible and total, the relief of a clerk finally allowed to correct the founding entry. “The Court's books are wrong from page one. I will say so at the crossover, before the Reels, before the rota, before whatever I am after the machine stands down. The dead deserve the erratum read aloud.”`)+((G.f.a4_audit=="published")?(P(`“Your audit reached the river sects with the wrong sum's worst half,” she adds, dry as dust. “Publish THIS half too, weaver. If my name is to be a curse downriver, let it at least be cursed for the correct entry.”`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`There is one record left to check, and it is yours.`,go:"a5c28_porch"}]};

SC["a5c28_porch"]={t:()=>P(`That night you go back through the index alone, to one page: your own.`)+P(`<i>Gold-aspect, riverbank intake, Azure Cloud watershed.</i> The thin-cloth charts agree: the mountain's province, fray-adjacent, a sky already wearing through when a transformer sang on another world's street corner. You were sent to a hole, like all the others. The arithmetic of heaven, nothing personal.`)+P(`Except. The Between sews loose stitches down GENTLY — you watched it do its work, dozens of souls, all of them placid, drifting, settling into torn cloth like snow. You didn't drift. You GRASPED${!G.f.grasped?" — or the thread, humming your name, settled over you like a weaver laying weft, which Suyin says is rarer still: the line choosing its stitch outright":""}. Your thread was the one thread in the dark already warm. Already humming. Already YOURS, before you died.`)+((G.f.bg=="sister")?(P(`And you know why. A porch light, kept burning, nightly, by a girl who never once got evidence. Love is thread — Suyin has been telling you all act; the recruiters wrote it about two sisters forty years ago; the whole Court runs on the woven kind. Hers ran off the world's edge, looking for you, and when the Between went hunting a stitch for a torn sky, it reached for the line that was already lit. The first stitch chose you back, golden boy. You were sent BECAUSE you were held.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="kata")?(P(`And you think you know why. Ten thousand repetitions of a form whose whole teaching was: be IN the world, not at it. A boy who trained his body to answer before fear could vote — when the Between went hunting a stitch strong enough for torn sky, it reached for a line already taut. The form chose you back. You were sent because you had spent years learning how to hold.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="music")?(P(`And you think you know why. Eight bars, unresolved, carried so long they'd worn a channel in you — a boy who could not put a melody down. Unfinished things hold HARDEST; every weaver knows it; a tied-off thread lies quiet but a live end REACHES. When the Between went hunting a stitch for torn sky, it took the line still reaching. The song chose you back. You were sent because you couldn't stop holding on.`)):(""))+((G.f.bg=="code")?(P(`And you think you know why. A pocket cube, a solving sequence, a boy who believed all the way down that broken states have PATHS back to order — that there is no scramble without a solution. The Between is, among its other natures, an optimizer. When it went hunting a stitch for torn sky, it took the line already convinced the tear could be solved. The premise chose you back. You were sent because you'd never once believed in unfixable.`)):(""))+P(`The debt runs both directions, then. The world owed you a sky that didn't eat you. You owe the Between one mended tear — not as payment. As the completion of the stitch it sewed.`)+SYS(`The ledger of heaven, balanced at last: foreign souls are sutures, sent where the sky is thinnest, and yours was chosen because something would not let go. Four days to the crossover. (a5_truth)`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The pattern needs its anchor-ring now: every thread you ever tied, gathered in one place.`,go:"a5c29_gather"}]};